    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d154">

                <pb facs="0151" n="137" xml:id="pg137"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.51/5072: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-09-02T18:00:00-04:00">September 2,
                            1942—6 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:12 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1418. Department’s No. 884, August 8, 6 p.m. Yesterday a decree was signed
                    prohibiting the importation, (except for $250 when approved by the Exchange
                    Control Commission) and holding of dollar currency by private persons or
                    transactions except with the knowledge and consent of the Central Bank. I am
                    awaiting a copy of the decree promised by the Foreign Office and will send brief
                    summary by cable.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d154-f1"/> Copy and translation by air
                        mail.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d154-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
